# The settings (environment variables) this starter needs. The values are secret, so this file holds
# only the names; you fill in the values yourself.
#
# - On Vercel: the import screen can fill in one row for every active line below. Those are exactly
#   the three you type in yourself. Connecting Neon (the database) and Blob (the image storage) later
#   adds their own settings automatically, so they are NOT active lines here: a second, empty row with
#   the same name would clash with theirs.
# - On your own computer: copy this file to .env.local (never commit .env.local: it holds secrets),
#   fill in the three values, and also remove the # in front of DATABASE_URL below and fill that in.

# A random text of at least 32 characters that you make up yourself (for example from a password
# manager). It signs log-ins and the links on the booking confirmation pages, and it scrambles the
# device addresses the request limits remember. It is never looked up anywhere, so any long random text
# works. Changing it later logs everyone out and makes earlier confirmation links stop working.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# The admin account this starter creates for you the first time it runs (a fresh database has no
# admin user yet, and no one else may create one - see docs/guides/local-setup.md). Pick any e-mail
# address and password; you will log in with them at /admin.
FIRST_ADMIN_EMAIL=
FIRST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ONLY in your .env.local, for local work: your own database's address, from your free Neon database
# (docs/guides/local-setup.md explains how). It looks like postgresql://user:password@host/dbname.
# Remove the # at the start of the next line, then paste the address after the = sign.
# On Vercel, leave it out: connecting Neon adds the address for you.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Optional: images are stored in Vercel Blob once you connect a Blob store in Vercel, which adds this
# setting for you. Without it, uploaded images are saved in the project's media folder, which only
# works on your own computer.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Optional: the members' area (log in at /account/login, "My bookings" at /account). It
# is off until this says exactly "on". Use it with test data only: made-up members and bookings. To
# switch it on: in Vercel, add the setting MEMBERS_AREA with the value on, then redeploy (on your own
# computer: remove the # below, then restart npm run dev). Editors create the member accounts in /admin.
# MEMBERS_AREA=on

# Optional: analytics (src/lib/analytics.ts). Off until this names a connected tool. To use Vercel Web
# Analytics: switch on Analytics in your Vercel project, add the setting NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS with the
# value vercel, then redeploy. On the free Hobby plan only page views are recorded; the site's two
# events (filter_used, booking_saved) need a paid plan. For another tool, see src/lib/analytics.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS=
